 !!! Note
     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Currency exposure limit
+
+If several of your pairs share the same underlying (quote/settlement) currency - for example a handful of BTC-margined futures, or several coins all quoted in the same stablecoin - a large adverse move in that one currency can hit multiple open trades at once, even though each trade looked fine in isolation.
+
+`max_currency_exposure` limits the combined stake committed, across all simultaneously open trades, to a single underlying currency, as a share of your total tradable capital.
+
+For example, with `max_currency_exposure=0.5` and a total tradable capital of 1000 USDT, at most 500 USDT may be committed at the same time to trades whose pair is quoted in USDT. Once that cap would be exceeded, a new trade in that currency is either sized down to fit under the limit, or - if the remaining allowance is below the pair's minimum tradable amount - not opened at all, the same way trades are already sized down or rejected when they exceed other stake limits (e.g. available balance or exchange minimums).
+
+This option is disabled by default (no cap). It's evaluated identically for live/dry-run and backtesting, since both use the same stake-sizing logic.
+
+!!! Note
+    This setting respects the [available balance configuration](#tradable-balance).
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
